  "summary": "MacSync is a macOS infostealer and backdoor family distributed under MaaS via fake crypto-wallet apps (e.g. Toria), malicious DMGs and iCloud calendar scripts. This version uses binary Objective-C/Swift droppers, AES-CBC/GCM-encrypted modules, ECDH Curve25519 key wrapping via the custom pkgunpack utility, and an HTTP C2 requiring the X-Upload-Token header. It steals browser, crypto-wallet and developer credentials, verifies the admin password via the PAM API, and persists through a com.apple.finder.agent LaunchAgent, .zshrc injection and Git hooks.",
